    {
      "id": "HTF-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Stabilizer transfer recovers the complementary share of the period",
      "anchor": "inputs-hecke-transfer-proof",
      "statement": "For a cycle stabilized from size n, the size N Hecke average is (1−I_n/I_N) times the original period plus (I_n/I_N) times its smaller-size Hecke average. Stabilizer vanishing applies to each complementary difference on its own stabilizer; their sum vanishes on the whole cycle.",
      "hypotheses": [
        "A totally complex arithmetic field, positive degree m<r₂, n≥1, r≥1, a principal prime (π), an arithmetic-invariant closed homogeneous cocycle F, a cycle z in size n, and the evaluation, transfer and affine-block inputs of pKey. The lower bound on the residue norm is needed for the separate contraction estimate."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-hecke-transfer-share"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "HTF-01",
        "AFB-02"
      ],
